560		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
561			<section aria-label="Introduction">
562				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
563				<p>
564					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
565					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
566				</p>
567				<p>
568					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
569					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
570				</p>
571			</section>
572	
573			<section aria-labelledby="features">
574				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
575				<ul>
576					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
577					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
578					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
579					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
580					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
581					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
582				</ul>
583			</section>
584	
585			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
586				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
587				<article class="card">
588					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
589					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
590					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
591				</article>
592	
593				<article class="card">
594					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
595					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. All interactive elements include visible focus indicators and proper ARIA labels.</p>
596					<p><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to move forward, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd> to move backward, and <kbd>Enter</kbd> to activate.</p>
597				</article>
598	
599				<article class="card">
600					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
601					<form id="contact-form" novalidate>
602						<p class="form-hint">Fields marked * are required.</p>
603						<div class="field">
604							<label for="email">Email <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
605							<input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="none" required aria-describedby="email-help">
606							<span id="email-error" class="error-message"></span>
607							<small id="email-help" class="form-hint">For example, name@example.com</small>
608						</div>
609						<div class="field">
610							<label for="message">Message</label>
611							<textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="message-help"></textarea>
612							<small id="message-help" class="form-hint">Up to 2,000 characters. <span id="message-count">2,000</span> remaining.</small>
613						</div>
614						<button type="submit">Send message</button>
615						<p id="form-status" role="status"></p>
616					</form>
617				</article>
